Z||000011||Fiero_24||09-18-2001||12:23 PM||||Those clear lenses are looking good!!!!  I cannot wait to see the GT ones when they are finished.<P>Haze, when are we going to try those 1/4 windows?  I made a test one and it looks good on plexiglass.  Its up to you if you want the black on the outside or the inside of the 1/4 window, I am just not sure if the black will peel off over time.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sunset_1_1_1.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
Z||000012||qwikgta||09-18-2001||08:53 PM||||Here is some more feedback,<P>I got the LED lights home today and I am going to have to do some mods to make them fit.  Just like my red lights these LED ones are for the 1157 bulbs not 2057 like we need.  If anyone can get LED for the 2057 then it may be worth trying.  I was able to get the bulb in far enough for it to light up and I didn't like the amount of light it put out.  It was not brighter just more concentrated at the center.  Will have to check it out at night to see if its worth moding.  <P>HAZE.. I got the wrong size piece of plactic.  I needed to get the larger size but I thought that the 2x2 would be enough to cover the lens.  I was only going to do the lens cover over the lights and blacken out the rest like you have.  I still can do it (and may) or get a larger piece to make one lens cover per piece. (good catch)<P>MinnGreen...I got this piece of plastic after reading your thread from last week, thanks for the idea.  I agree without it they just look unfinished.  <P>FalconHulk... yes it is a Supertrapp.  I have it mounted up to a straight (shaped) pipe attached to a hooker header.  More pics and info on my webpage in signature<P>Sootah.. my first set were Chrome painted and had no "Stryene" in front of it.  I broke them trying to make this set.  I did not paint this set but I didnt glue this one together so if I want to I can open it up again and paint it.  I may do this or paint the inside lens to blacken it out.  <P>Thanks<P>Rob<P><P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroMaster88||09-21-2001||12:09 AM||||I have 2 questions:<BR>1.  How did you cut them without breaking the sheets?  I was thinkin of useing my dremel..seems to be a good idea I think.  <P>2.  How did you get the pieces to fit purfect?  Where did you get the mesurements from?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">             <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||5
Z||000014||Haze_Performance||09-21-2001||01:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>Haze, when are we going to try those 1/4 windows?  I made a test one and it looks good on plexiglass.  Its up to you if you want the black on the outside or the inside of the 1/4 window, I am just not sure if the black will peel off over time.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I found a set of 84 glass ones to put on.. Thanks anyway...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">    .    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">    .    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole_6_2.gif">        <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000015||Fformula88||09-21-2001||10:39 AM||||They look good!  Great job!||||reg||1
Z||000016||MinnGreenGT||09-21-2001||10:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>I have 2 questions:<BR>1.  How did you cut them without breaking the sheets?  I was thinkin of useing my dremel..seems to be a good idea I think.  <P>2.  How did you get the pieces to fit purfect?  Where did you get the mesurements from?<P>Thanks!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1. If you read the tag on the image at the top of the post, it recommends cutting/scoring the smooth side, then snapping it off over a solid edge (that's what I've been doing for my GT lenses).  I do use my Dremel for rounding rough edges though.<P>2. As for the shape, I initially used a piece of paper or cardboard... cut it to fit, then trace it onto the plastic using a sharpie marker or similiar.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroMaster88||09-21-2001||01:32 PM||||Thanks MinnGreenGT.  Thats what I was gonna do.  Just wanted to make sure that was the best way to go. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">             <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||14
Z||000018||qwikgta||09-22-2001||01:47 AM||||Sorry for not getting back sooner.  I too made a templete and then used a marker on the plastic.  I cut it a little big and then kept trimming it down to size.  Then I epoxyed the corners to keep it from moving.  <P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000019||My7Fieros||09-22-2001||03:30 PM||||I actually like it! Looks good! Sorry, but that exhaust is really distracting though..I'd do away w/it personally, but the lights look good!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||7
